      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T21:46:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This CL breaks backcompat, and it will also break native\u003c-\u003eJava transactions. Internal bug b/172502290 has some prior work moving towards this.\n\nAnyway, I spent some time a few years ago starting to do this, but I never found the time to finish it. What you would have to consider:\n- making this work in libbinder (C++/Rust) not just Java\n- app backcompat (some apps freeze the format)\n- utf-8 is only common in some regions (utf encoding may be less efficient for certain strings)\n- converting to utf-8 will require extra allocations in some places, likely have to support both (e.g. write \u00271\u0027 if utf-8 or \u00272\u0027 if utf-16)\n- RPC binder code needs to be backwards compatible\n\nSo, there is quite a significant amount of work this would take.",
      "parentUuid": "3f76fa15_33dbb07c",
      "revId": "0e134518a3f69128718ae979abf2ad6a75d6848c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
